      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. The `GATT_PERM_*` masks are additive - i.e. if we have `GATT_PERM_READ_ENCRYPTED` and `GATT_PERM_WRITE`, then we can BOTH read-if-encrypted and unconditionally write.\n\nThus, if we match READ_IF_DISCOVERABLE, and are discoverable, then we should succeed.\n\nThe reason these checks appear to be subtractive, is because they are comparing against these \"composite\" bitmasks: https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/+/refs/heads/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/include/gatt_api.h;l\u003d293\n\nI don\u0027t know why they do that, but the behavior is the same as if we checked against the masks directly.",
